flickos-screenshot (1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The markup window: a click on a screenshot's notification, or
    `flickos-screenshot edit FILE`, opens it to draw on it (pen,
    highlighter, arrow, box, text), hide something with a solid box, or
    crop it, with undo and redo and zoom, then copy it or save it. One
    window per session. New Screenshot in it runs the bar with only
    Photo (`bar --photo`).

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:27:34 +0800

flickos-screenshot (1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * After a screenshot, the shutter sound plays and what was taken
    flashes white, unless the desktop's event sounds or animations are
    off; Do Not Disturb silences the sound. The flash's child starts
    before the grab, so it is ready when the picture is, and the next
    grab waits for its flash.

